{number: 80}
{title: Onward, Christian Soldiers}
{key: Eb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Eb] Onward, Christian soldiers, marching as to [Bb7] war,
With the cross of [Eb] Jesus going on be-[Bb7] fore.
[Eb] Christ, the royal Master, leads a-[Ab] gainst the [Eb] foe;
Forward into [Ab] battle [Eb] see His [Bb7] banners [Eb] go!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Eb] Onward, Christian soldiers, marching as to [Bb7] war,
With the cross of [Eb] Jesus [Ab] going [Eb] on [Bb7] be-[Eb] fore.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Eb] At the sign of triumph Satan's host doth [Bb7] flee;
On, then, Christian [Eb] soldiers, on to victo-[Bb7] ry!
[Eb] Hell's foundations quiver at the [Ab] shout of [Eb] praise;
Brothers, lift your [Ab] voices, [Eb] loud your [Bb7] anthems [Eb] raise!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Eb] Like a mighty army moves the Church of [Bb7] God;
Brothers, we are [Eb] treading where the saints have [Bb7] trod.
[Eb] We are not divided; all one [Ab] body [Eb] we,
One in hope and [Ab] doctrine, [Eb] one in [Bb7] chari-[Eb] ty.
{end_of_verse}
